<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<configuration>

  <!--
    Two sources, and a <clear /> so that those two are the ONLY ones.

    Without the clear, a restore resolves against whatever sources happen to be configured on the
    machine doing it. That is how a public repository quietly acquires a dependency nobody else can
    restore: it builds on the author's box, from a feed only the author can reach, and fails for
    everyone else with a package-not-found that names no reason. CI and a laptop should agree, and
    saying what the sources are is the only way to make them agree.

    A project that genuinely needs a third feed adds it itself and says why: samples/WebLlvm asks
    for the experimental ILC feed through RestoreAdditionalProjectSources, which is additive to
    this file and stays scoped to the one project that needs it.
  -->
  <packageSources>
    <clear />
    <add key="nuget.org" value="https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json" />
    <add key="GitHub-Wixely-Packages" value="https://nuget.pkg.github.com/Wixely/index.json" />
  </packageSources>

  <!--
    NO CREDENTIALS HERE, deliberately, and it is worth knowing why you may still need some.

    GitHub Packages requires authentication to RESTORE a NuGet package, including a public one,
    unlike its npm and Maven registries which serve public packages anonymously. So the Khalkos3D
    engine, though it is MIT and its repository is public, cannot be fetched by an anonymous build.

    In CI the workflow supplies the built-in GITHUB_TOKEN for this source, so nothing is needed
    there. Locally, run `dotnet nuget update source GitHub-Wixely-Packages` once, passing your
    GitHub username and a personal access token with read:packages scope (the username, password
    and store-password-in-clear-text options). That writes to your USER level NuGet config and
    never to this file, which is why this file has no credentials section for a token to be
    committed into by accident.

    Only samples/Khalkos3dBridge needs the engine, so a machine with no token still restores and
    builds everything else in the repository.
  -->

</configuration>
